# claude-sel prompts — one verb per line:
#
#   <key> <name> <prompt text...>
#
# key    single character; becomes the StumpWM key in *claude-sel-map*
#        ("-" = no key, only reachable via the dmenu picker / CLI).
#        Avoid SPC and the C-<x> prefixes used by claude-sel.lisp.
# name   used on the command line: `claude-sel <name>`
# prompt the instruction given to Claude. The selected text is the input.
#        The special prompt "?" asks for an ad-hoc instruction via dmenu.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. After editing,
# run the StumpWM command `claude-sel-reload` to rebuild the keymap.

g fix-german  Correct grammar, spelling and punctuation of this German text. Keep the meaning, wording and tone as close to the original as possible; change only what is wrong.
e english     Translate this text into natural, idiomatic English. Keep tone and formatting.
m email       Rewrite this as a concise, professional email. Keep the language of the input (German stays German). Keep all facts; drop filler. No subject line unless the input has one.
s summarize   Summarize this text in a few short bullet points. Use the language of the input.
x explain     Explain this text plainly and briefly: what it means and anything non-obvious. Use the language of the input.
f free        ?
